tags: call, mu_per_call

A rate of a service: the price of one call to a method of the slot. The service
charges it to the caller, not the node.

The value is MU for one call. Example: 10. A call is one request of the protocol of
the slot (for example one gRPC call).

The scope is the name of the method, as UTF-8, as the protocol of the slot names it.
An empty scope is the general rate for each call. The node does not read this rate.

=== formal
base=one call
